    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d213">

                <pb facs="0175" n="163" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg163"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.20 Defense/19<hi rendition="#superscript"
                        >11/14</hi>: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Uruguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Montevideo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-06-22T14:00:00-03:30">June 22, 1940—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 3:35 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>122. Reference my 115, June 18, 5 p.m.<anchor n="30" xml:id="d213-f1"/> The
                    conversations have gone very well. Reports by air mail today.<anchor n="31"
                        xml:id="d213-f2"/></p>
                <p>Colonel Wooten left for Santiago June 20 and Captain Spears left for Buenos Aires
                    yesterday.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
